WEBVTT

00:00:13.360 --> 00:00:15.406
I'm so zonked.

00:00:15.449 --> 00:00:17.277
The red alerts
from that wormhole

00:00:17.321 --> 00:00:19.453
-kept me up half the night.
-Oh, I know.

00:00:19.497 --> 00:00:21.629
It's, like, are we crossing
the event horizon or not?

00:00:21.673 --> 00:00:24.371
Like, I don't care, actually.
I just want you to pick one.

00:00:24.415 --> 00:00:26.069
Jet. What are you doing here?

00:00:26.112 --> 00:00:27.374
Got reassigned to Beta shift.

00:00:27.418 --> 00:00:29.333
Looks like
we'll be showering together.

00:00:29.376 --> 00:00:30.899
Cool. Well, welcome to the team.

00:00:30.943 --> 00:00:32.597
I'm sort of
the unofficial leader.

00:00:32.640 --> 00:00:35.556
Feel free to come to me
with any questions.

00:00:35.600 --> 00:00:36.949
She's joking, right?

00:00:36.992 --> 00:00:38.994
Nope.

00:00:45.436 --> 00:00:47.699
Ooh, actually, usually Boimler
leaves that one open for me.

00:00:47.742 --> 00:00:49.701
He has issues
with communal nudity.

00:00:49.744 --> 00:00:52.182
Well, I'm not him,
and he's not here.

00:00:52.225 --> 00:00:54.836
Cool. Hope this isn't
too high for you.

00:00:56.273 --> 00:00:58.057
-Ooh! Ha-ha! Fine with me.

00:00:58.101 --> 00:00:59.841
-I could go higher.

00:00:59.885 --> 00:01:03.062
-Uh, that's a little high,
don't you think?

00:01:03.106 --> 00:01:04.542
-Not for me!
-This is my favorite!

00:01:07.414 --> 00:01:09.155
-I think I'm clean!
-Yeah, I'm good!

00:01:09.199 --> 00:01:12.593
I could do this all day!

00:01:12.637 --> 00:01:14.813
Never felt more alive!

00:02:28.843 --> 00:02:33.326
&lt;i&gt;Captain's log, stardate 58001.2.&lt;/i&gt;

00:02:33.370 --> 00:02:35.067
&lt;i&gt;Those who spend their lives
and fortunes&lt;/i&gt;

00:02:35.110 --> 00:02:37.635
&lt;i&gt;gathering scientific rarities
from around the galaxy&lt;/i&gt;

00:02:37.678 --> 00:02:39.811
&lt;i&gt;call themselves "collectors."&lt;/i&gt;

00:02:39.854 --> 00:02:42.030
&lt;i&gt;Now, a prominent collector
has died,&lt;/i&gt;

00:02:42.074 --> 00:02:45.860
&lt;i&gt;leaving behind a starship full
of hazardous treasures that need&lt;/i&gt;

00:02:45.904 --> 00:02:47.427
&lt;i&gt;to be safely catalogued.&lt;/i&gt;

00:02:47.471 --> 00:02:50.517
&lt;i&gt;The Collector's Guild has asked
the Federation for help,&lt;/i&gt;

00:02:50.561 --> 00:02:53.041
&lt;i&gt;so the&lt;/i&gt; Cerritos &lt;i&gt;
has been tasked with the job.&lt;/i&gt;

00:02:53.085 --> 00:02:56.131
Chairman Siggi, allow me
to offer my deepest condolences

00:02:56.175 --> 00:02:58.133
for the loss of your friend.

00:02:58.177 --> 00:02:59.657
&lt;i&gt;Kerner Hauze was no friend.&lt;/i&gt;

00:02:59.700 --> 00:03:02.486
&lt;i&gt;His collection pales
in comparison to mine.&lt;/i&gt;

00:03:02.529 --> 00:03:04.270
Well, I'm sure that's true.

00:03:04.314 --> 00:03:05.880
How can we help?

00:03:05.924 --> 00:03:07.708
&lt;i&gt;Well, I'm supposed
to auction off his things,&lt;/i&gt;

00:03:07.752 --> 00:03:09.710
&lt;i&gt;per Guild rules,
but I don't know&lt;/i&gt;

00:03:09.754 --> 00:03:11.756
&lt;i&gt;what kind of dangerous items
he might have been hoarding.&lt;/i&gt;

00:03:11.799 --> 00:03:14.541
&lt;i&gt;I need you guys to come in
and safely dispose of anything&lt;/i&gt;

00:03:14.585 --> 00:03:16.674
&lt;i&gt;that could,
you know, atomize me.&lt;/i&gt;

00:03:16.717 --> 00:03:18.676
Happy to help.
We'll prepare a team.

00:03:18.719 --> 00:03:21.374
&lt;i&gt;And I'll be overseein' 'em--
I don't want any of your crew&lt;/i&gt;

00:03:21.418 --> 00:03:23.724
&lt;i&gt;getting sticky appendages.&lt;/i&gt;

00:03:23.768 --> 00:03:25.509
Ugh, Collector's Guild.

00:03:25.552 --> 00:03:26.901
Just a bunch of greedy packrats.

00:03:26.945 --> 00:03:29.034
Wasn't he the one
who tried to collect Data?

00:03:29.077 --> 00:03:30.731
They all tried to collect Data.

00:03:30.775 --> 00:03:32.385
Why couldn't they
leave Data alone?

00:03:32.429 --> 00:03:33.821
He just wanted to feel.

00:03:33.865 --> 00:03:35.823
This is the last thing I need
right now.

00:03:35.867 --> 00:03:37.956
I'm supposed
to find out the results

00:03:37.999 --> 00:03:39.566
of my command evaluation today.

00:03:39.610 --> 00:03:41.133
Well, sounds like
your basic tag-and-bag.

00:03:41.176 --> 00:03:42.352
Want me to head it up?

00:03:42.395 --> 00:03:44.484
No, I think
this is a fine first job

00:03:44.528 --> 00:03:46.704
for our brand-new
head of security.

00:03:49.402 --> 00:03:52.579
Lieutenant Kayshon,
welcome to the &lt;i&gt;Cerritos.&lt;/i&gt;

00:03:52.623 --> 00:03:55.626
Rapunki,
when he joined the seven.

00:03:57.105 --> 00:04:00.152
Ah, sorry. The universal
translator doesn't always...

00:04:00.195 --> 00:04:02.154
What I meant was, uh,

00:04:02.197 --> 00:04:04.765
"It is my honor, Captain."

00:04:04.809 --> 00:04:06.289
Jah! This is so cool!

00:04:06.332 --> 00:04:08.291
Lieutenant Kayshon is
the first Tamarian in Starfleet

00:04:08.334 --> 00:04:10.510
and we get to go on a mission
with him!

00:04:10.554 --> 00:04:13.470
Eh. We're basically clearing out
a dead dude's storage locker.

00:04:13.513 --> 00:04:16.081
A mission's only as important
as you make it, Mariner.

00:04:16.124 --> 00:04:17.909
Okay, Commander Protocol.

00:04:17.952 --> 00:04:19.954
-You always this fun?
-We're on the clock.

00:04:19.998 --> 00:04:22.348
I'll have fun &lt;i&gt;
after&lt;/i&gt; we do the job.

00:04:22.392 --> 00:04:24.350
Ugh. You sound uptighter
than Boimler.

00:04:24.394 --> 00:04:26.700
Ah, man, Boims would have loved
this mission.

00:04:26.744 --> 00:04:28.702
He took Ethics of Collecting
at the Academy.

00:04:28.746 --> 00:04:30.617
Yeah, but the &lt;i&gt;Titan's
such a big deal.&lt;/i&gt;

00:04:30.661 --> 00:04:32.489
I bet he's living the dream.

00:04:35.274 --> 00:04:37.058
Mr. Boimler,
attack pattern Delta.

00:04:37.102 --> 00:04:38.712
Target the aft shields.

00:04:38.756 --> 00:04:41.149
Let's see how these Pakleds do
with their aft hanging out.

00:04:41.193 --> 00:04:43.369
Uh, yes, sir.

00:04:49.984 --> 00:04:52.378
-Photon torpedoes locked
and ready.
-Fire!

00:04:56.164 --> 00:04:58.079
&lt;i&gt;Yeah!&lt;/i&gt;

00:04:58.123 --> 00:05:00.168
&lt;i&gt;Hasta mañana,&lt;/i&gt; Pakleds!

00:05:00.212 --> 00:05:03.389
-Great job, everyone.
That's a wrap.

00:05:06.044 --> 00:05:07.698
Lieutenant Kayshon,

00:05:07.741 --> 00:05:09.656
we're your away team,
reporting for duty.

00:05:09.700 --> 00:05:12.311
It is a pleasure to meet you,
and I look forward to, uh--

00:05:12.355 --> 00:05:15.183
oh, geez--
Darmok and Jalad on the ocean...

00:05:15.227 --> 00:05:16.402
"Working with you"?

00:05:16.446 --> 00:05:18.273
Yes! Thank you.

00:05:18.317 --> 00:05:21.189
Apologies, my Federation
Standard is still shaky.

00:05:21.233 --> 00:05:23.496
It's no problem, sir.
Or should I say,

00:05:23.540 --> 00:05:25.672
-it's no "beast at Tanagra."
Oh!

00:05:25.716 --> 00:05:27.892
More like suck-up at Tanagra.

00:05:32.592 --> 00:05:34.725
About time, Starfleet.

00:05:34.768 --> 00:05:37.858
What'd you do, stop to debate
the human rights of a robot?

00:05:37.902 --> 00:05:39.338
I-I do not believe so.

00:05:39.382 --> 00:05:40.861
Perhaps we should review
our logs.

00:05:40.905 --> 00:05:43.342
Hey, just bustin' your bioducts.
Here's the deal.

00:05:43.386 --> 00:05:45.997
I need youse to comb through all
this stuff on the floor here.

00:05:46.040 --> 00:05:48.173
But the high-ticket items
in these cases?

00:05:48.216 --> 00:05:50.131
That stuff stays here.

00:05:50.175 --> 00:05:51.829
Uh, okay.

00:05:51.872 --> 00:05:54.658
All right, if we split up, we
can knock this out in an hour.

00:05:54.701 --> 00:05:56.964
Whoa, big fella.
This is just the first room.

00:05:57.008 --> 00:05:59.402
Most of the collection's
further in the ship.

00:05:59.445 --> 00:06:00.620
There's more?

00:06:00.664 --> 00:06:02.317
Oh, how much
can one guy collect?

00:06:02.361 --> 00:06:04.319
Sister, you got no idea.

00:06:06.278 --> 00:06:07.932
&lt;i&gt;There's a pattern&lt;/i&gt;

00:06:07.975 --> 00:06:09.716
to the Pakleds' attacks
on these outposts.

00:06:09.760 --> 00:06:11.109
They're after Varuvian ore.

00:06:11.152 --> 00:06:12.893
Uh, s-sorry. What ore?

00:06:12.937 --> 00:06:15.200
Varuvian. Contains minerals
which become volatile

00:06:15.243 --> 00:06:17.071
at high vibratory frequencies.

00:06:17.115 --> 00:06:20.771
Those terrorists tried to use it
to blow up Starbase 58.

00:06:20.814 --> 00:06:22.860
Oh, uh, yeah,
I think I remember reading that

00:06:22.903 --> 00:06:23.991
in one of your logs.

00:06:24.035 --> 00:06:25.732
Huh. &lt;i&gt;Titan's&lt;/i&gt; seen
a lot of action.

00:06:25.776 --> 00:06:27.255
Ain't weaponizing Varuvian ore

00:06:27.299 --> 00:06:29.040
a bit above
the Pakleds' grade level?

00:06:29.083 --> 00:06:31.434
Way above, which is
why Starfleet Command believes

00:06:31.477 --> 00:06:33.523
there may be
another player involved.

00:06:33.566 --> 00:06:35.394
Intel says
the Pakleds' next target

00:06:35.438 --> 00:06:37.831
is a Varuvian mining colony
on Karzill IV.

00:06:37.875 --> 00:06:39.833
We'll embed an away team there
disguised as miners

00:06:39.877 --> 00:06:41.835
with the goal
of planting a tracking device

00:06:41.879 --> 00:06:43.184
on their shuttle.

00:06:43.228 --> 00:06:45.317
They'll lead us
right to their puppet master.

00:06:45.360 --> 00:06:47.319
And that's
when we cut the strings.

00:06:47.362 --> 00:06:50.409
-Cutting the strings.
-You don't have
to write that down.

00:06:50.453 --> 00:06:53.891
I don't have to write that down.

00:06:57.155 --> 00:06:59.679
Got another
old disintegrator here.

00:06:59.723 --> 00:07:02.726
Oh, hey, Cyborg.
You're pretty rare, huh?

00:07:02.769 --> 00:07:05.511
Yeah, as far as I know there's
only a few of us in Starfleet.

00:07:05.555 --> 00:07:06.991
Interesting.

00:07:07.034 --> 00:07:08.601
Careful, Ruthy,
he's gonna try to collect you.

00:07:08.645 --> 00:07:10.081
-Take my card.

00:07:10.124 --> 00:07:12.083
I got a top-notch menagerie.

00:07:13.388 --> 00:07:17.131
So, Kerner Hauze just lived here
all alone on an automated ship?

00:07:17.175 --> 00:07:18.959
He must have been so lonely.

00:07:19.003 --> 00:07:21.484
Perhaps to him
the silence was, uh...

00:07:21.527 --> 00:07:23.747
"Temba, his arms open."

00:07:23.790 --> 00:07:25.531
-A gift?
-Yes, gift. Sorry.

00:07:25.575 --> 00:07:27.402
Perhaps he preferred
to be alone.

00:07:27.446 --> 00:07:29.796
Yeah, I guess more time
to enjoy...

00:07:29.840 --> 00:07:32.320
"Kahless' fornication helmet."

00:07:32.364 --> 00:07:34.279
Oh, that's fun. Safety first.

00:07:34.322 --> 00:07:37.978
This way, mortals,
or thou shalt be smited.

00:07:38.022 --> 00:07:40.372
We got a lot to do.
You might want to focus.

00:07:40.415 --> 00:07:42.156
And you might want
to loosen up.

00:07:42.200 --> 00:07:44.637
Oh, yeah, loosen up
while carrying ordnance--

00:07:44.681 --> 00:07:46.421
great idea, Mariner.

00:07:48.598 --> 00:07:50.338
Whoa! Uh, what's going on?

00:07:50.382 --> 00:07:52.166
-Ah-ah-ah.

00:07:52.210 --> 00:07:55.343
If you're seeing this
holo-message, it means I'm dead

00:07:55.387 --> 00:07:59.522
and you're trying to steal
from my precious collection.

00:07:59.565 --> 00:08:01.654
Oh-ho, great!
Automated defenses!

00:08:01.698 --> 00:08:03.787
-You must've moved something.
-What?!

00:08:03.830 --> 00:08:06.050
You had us move lots of things!

00:08:06.093 --> 00:08:07.486
For your greed,

00:08:07.530 --> 00:08:10.707
you will now be part
of my collection!

00:08:19.890 --> 00:08:21.021
-Lieutenant Kayshon!

00:08:21.065 --> 00:08:23.458
Help me! It's-it's...

00:08:23.502 --> 00:08:25.852
"Zinda, his eyes red!"

00:08:25.896 --> 00:08:27.158
He's saying, "It hurts."

00:08:27.201 --> 00:08:29.290
Yeah, man, I get it.
Context clues.

00:08:32.903 --> 00:08:34.513
That beam
turned him into a puppet!

00:08:34.557 --> 00:08:35.862
He'll be worth a fortune.

00:08:35.906 --> 00:08:38.169
Could you stop collecting
for one...

00:08:38.212 --> 00:08:39.387
Aah, flying orb!

00:08:50.442 --> 00:08:53.271
Whoa!
Manhaver to &lt;i&gt;Cerritos,&lt;/i&gt; come in.

00:08:53.314 --> 00:08:57.057
-Comms are blocked.
-We've got to get out
of here! Now!

00:09:01.888 --> 00:09:03.194
I've got him.
No,

00:09:03.237 --> 00:09:04.717
&lt;i&gt;-I've&lt;/i&gt; got him.
Guys!

00:09:05.892 --> 00:09:08.155
-Out of my way.
-Hey!
-Let's go.

00:09:11.594 --> 00:09:14.945
I told you to keep your hands
to yourself, Orion.

00:09:14.988 --> 00:09:16.381
-Just great.

00:09:16.424 --> 00:09:19.340
This is what I get
for involving Starfleet.

00:09:19.384 --> 00:09:21.429
Oh, you want to try
to get through the killer ship

00:09:21.473 --> 00:09:23.083
on your own? Be my guest.

00:09:23.127 --> 00:09:26.043
-Oh, man,
it's just gallery after gallery.
-We need to get

00:09:26.086 --> 00:09:28.045
to the engine room
and disable the defenses.

00:09:28.088 --> 00:09:29.873
For us to make it out of here,
we're gonna have to travel

00:09:29.916 --> 00:09:32.571
-into the belly of the beast.
-Quiet. I've got a safer plan.

00:09:32.615 --> 00:09:35.313
What? No, you don't cut off
my badass plan.

00:09:35.356 --> 00:09:37.532
-Not even Boimler would...
-Shh. He's gone.

00:09:37.576 --> 00:09:39.056
Get over it. Now listen.

00:09:39.099 --> 00:09:40.666
There are escape pods
right here.

00:09:40.710 --> 00:09:43.364
And fewer galleries
to go through means better odds.

00:09:43.408 --> 00:09:45.018
We don't need
to be heroes today, people.

00:09:45.062 --> 00:09:46.454
We just need to survive.

00:09:46.498 --> 00:09:48.239
-I'm with the hunk.
-You don't get a vote.

00:09:48.282 --> 00:09:50.763
Uh, actually,
I think I like Jet's plan, too.

00:09:50.807 --> 00:09:52.852
Tendi. Okay, Rutherford,
what about you?

00:09:52.896 --> 00:09:54.593
Yeah, it just sounds less risky?

00:09:54.637 --> 00:09:56.421
It's more like
what our training says to do.

00:09:56.464 --> 00:09:58.684
Exactly.
If we follow our training,

00:09:58.728 --> 00:10:01.687
we get out of here alive.
All of us.

00:10:03.820 --> 00:10:05.648
&lt;i&gt;Ooh,&lt;/i&gt;

00:10:05.691 --> 00:10:07.258
I love me an undercover op.

00:10:07.301 --> 00:10:08.651
You could tell
the captain was bummed

00:10:08.694 --> 00:10:09.826
to have to stay on the ship.

00:10:09.869 --> 00:10:11.262
Badass like Riker,

00:10:11.305 --> 00:10:13.394
you know he'd rather
have boots on the ground.

00:10:13.438 --> 00:10:15.353
He must have been so bored
on the &lt;i&gt;Enterprise.&lt;/i&gt;

00:10:15.396 --> 00:10:18.051
I mean,
seven years of what, exploring?

00:10:18.095 --> 00:10:20.663
On a ship
with five day care centers.

00:10:20.706 --> 00:10:22.926
Are you talking about the &lt;i&gt;D?
The flagship?&lt;/i&gt;

00:10:22.969 --> 00:10:24.275
They went
to different dimensions.

00:10:24.318 --> 00:10:26.103
They fought the Borg.
They insurrected.

00:10:26.146 --> 00:10:27.713
They had
regular string quartets.

00:10:27.757 --> 00:10:30.020
-Wow, what a rush.

00:10:30.063 --> 00:10:31.891
Play me a concerto.

00:10:31.935 --> 00:10:34.067
That's dumb.

00:10:36.809 --> 00:10:38.681
Uh, Captain?

00:10:38.724 --> 00:10:39.725
You feeling okay?

00:10:39.769 --> 00:10:41.640
Hmm? I'm fine. Why?

00:10:41.684 --> 00:10:43.947
This is typically about the time
you'd start asking

00:10:43.990 --> 00:10:46.036
for a second
or even third status report

00:10:46.079 --> 00:10:47.385
from the away team, but, uh,

00:10:47.428 --> 00:10:49.126
you haven't even asked
for one yet.

00:10:49.169 --> 00:10:52.216
Commander, are you suggesting
that I micromanage?

00:10:52.259 --> 00:10:54.044
-No, no, no. Not at all. I...
-Because that &lt;i&gt;is&lt;/i&gt;

00:10:54.087 --> 00:10:56.133
what Starfleet Command
said in my evaluation.

00:10:56.176 --> 00:10:57.308
Can you believe that?

00:10:57.351 --> 00:11:00.180
Since when do I micromanage?

00:11:01.007 --> 00:11:05.446
I am going to have to "show
more trust in my subordinates."

00:11:05.490 --> 00:11:09.973
Lieutenant Kayshon
is an accomplished officer.

00:11:10.016 --> 00:11:12.671
I am sure
he's got a handle on things.

00:11:16.066 --> 00:11:18.024
Rutherford, take the puppet.

00:11:18.068 --> 00:11:20.635
-Tendi, target the hinge.

00:11:26.990 --> 00:11:28.382
Inorganic matter compactor!

00:11:28.426 --> 00:11:31.429
-Whoa! Whoa!
-Rutherford!

00:11:32.256 --> 00:11:34.998
-Don't let go!

00:11:35.041 --> 00:11:36.434
Hey, what the [bleep]?!
Little help?

00:11:36.477 --> 00:11:38.044
Not my problem!

00:11:51.449 --> 00:11:54.495
Huh?
Whoa.

00:11:55.279 --> 00:11:57.890
Hey! Thanks
for helping out back there.

00:11:57.934 --> 00:11:59.370
You couldn't lend
a frickin' tentacle?

00:11:59.413 --> 00:12:02.373
-Get your lousy hands off me.

00:12:02.416 --> 00:12:05.158
Kahless's sex helmet?
You took it!

00:12:05.202 --> 00:12:06.638
That's what set off the ship!

00:12:06.681 --> 00:12:09.554
This is all your fault,
you pervert! No judgment.

00:12:09.597 --> 00:12:10.729
Oh, save it, Orion.

00:12:10.773 --> 00:12:12.775
I don't got to answer
to nobody but me.

00:12:12.818 --> 00:12:16.604
That's how I got on top,
that's how I'm staying on top.

00:12:16.648 --> 00:12:17.867
Don't move.

00:12:17.910 --> 00:12:19.259
I'm done
listening to youse.

00:12:23.002 --> 00:12:25.135
Maybe his helmet saved him?

00:12:27.920 --> 00:12:29.704
Guess we have
to go up and over.

00:12:34.318 --> 00:12:37.930
Uh, remind me again
how this was the safer option?

00:12:37.974 --> 00:12:40.106
There's unknowns to any plan.

00:12:40.150 --> 00:12:42.065
If we'd gone your way,
we'd have had to fight

00:12:42.108 --> 00:12:43.544
twice as many collectables

00:12:43.588 --> 00:12:46.069
&lt;i&gt;and&lt;/i&gt; free-climb
a radiation coolant pipe.

00:12:46.112 --> 00:12:47.679
I'm not afraid of a little risk.

00:12:47.722 --> 00:12:49.812
-But what about them?

00:12:49.855 --> 00:12:51.204
Maybe you've got a death wish,

00:12:51.248 --> 00:12:53.119
but you can't ask them
to follow you there.

00:12:53.163 --> 00:12:54.773
Oh, don't act like
you're watching out for them.

00:12:54.817 --> 00:12:57.428
You're just using them
to prop yourself up.

00:12:57.471 --> 00:12:59.430
What are you talking about?

00:12:59.473 --> 00:13:02.172
You want everyone to see you
as this big, brave hero

00:13:02.215 --> 00:13:03.913
who only cares
about the team, but...

00:13:03.956 --> 00:13:06.089
-Oh, God, get out of here.
Stupid vacuum.

00:13:08.526 --> 00:13:11.268
Uh-oh. I think you triggered
some kind of network response.

00:13:11.311 --> 00:13:13.574
Aw, what are they gonna do,
suck us to death?

00:13:13.618 --> 00:13:15.838
Ow!

00:13:15.881 --> 00:13:17.970
They're gonna suck us to death!

00:13:20.233 --> 00:13:22.322
There's too many of them!

00:13:29.982 --> 00:13:31.288
We need a barricade.

00:13:31.331 --> 00:13:33.464
No, guys, grab a bone.
Just swing on 'em.

00:13:33.507 --> 00:13:35.814
-No, help me build.
-Don't listen to him.

00:13:35.858 --> 00:13:38.469
-Stand down, Mariner. &lt;i&gt;
-You&lt;/i&gt; stand down.

00:13:38.512 --> 00:13:40.514
-I told you to stand down.
You stand down.
-Uh...

00:13:44.518 --> 00:13:48.087
We are strong.
We take your mine.

00:13:48.131 --> 00:13:50.698
It is our mine now.

00:13:53.484 --> 00:13:56.052
Stay strong, brother.
We miners shall overcome.

00:13:56.095 --> 00:13:57.444
Dude, you're clearly Starfleet.

00:13:57.488 --> 00:13:58.837
Your hands are super soft
and clean.

00:13:58.881 --> 00:14:00.926
Uh, no, I'm a miner
with a heart of gold.

00:14:00.970 --> 00:14:02.493
And I have dad issues.

00:14:02.536 --> 00:14:04.495
Okay, the Pakleds' shuttle
is unattended. Now's our chance.

00:14:04.538 --> 00:14:06.584
Hold it.
We got a 'Led over there.

00:14:07.411 --> 00:14:08.934
We have to stun him,
or he could sound

00:14:08.978 --> 00:14:10.370
-the alarm.
-But our orders are to avoid...

00:14:10.414 --> 00:14:11.981
We can't leave anything
up to chance.

00:14:12.024 --> 00:14:13.808
Oh.

00:14:18.378 --> 00:14:20.990
Sorry, pal,
but this ain't your lucky...

00:14:21.033 --> 00:14:22.339
Huh?

00:14:22.382 --> 00:14:23.688
It's a pile of snacks.

00:14:23.731 --> 00:14:27.126
Hey! Those miners
are stealing our snacks.

00:14:27.170 --> 00:14:28.693
We're blown!

00:14:28.736 --> 00:14:31.217
Fall back to that tunnel!

00:14:35.569 --> 00:14:37.876
There,
this should buy us some time.

00:14:37.920 --> 00:14:39.356
I'll try to come up with a plan.

00:14:39.399 --> 00:14:41.401
Enough with this whole
textbook leader routine.

00:14:41.445 --> 00:14:42.794
We're not buying it.

00:14:42.837 --> 00:14:43.969
I'm just trying to step up here.

00:14:44.013 --> 00:14:45.405
&lt;i&gt;You're&lt;/i&gt; the one with the act.

00:14:45.449 --> 00:14:47.538
The whole
"dive in headfirst" thing.

00:14:47.581 --> 00:14:50.497
You're just desperate to be seen
as some kind of renegade hero.

00:14:50.541 --> 00:14:53.283
No, I'm not. Diving in
is just how I work best.

00:14:53.326 --> 00:14:54.937
And I like to think things out.

00:14:54.980 --> 00:14:57.548
Sorry if that comes off
all "textbook" to you.

00:14:57.591 --> 00:15:00.377
What, you think I'm trying to be
like Ransom up in here?

00:15:00.420 --> 00:15:02.683
Square jaw, all squinting,
like, "Let's roll"?

00:15:02.727 --> 00:15:04.903
Uh, no, not a good look.

00:15:04.947 --> 00:15:07.993
I'm just surprised that you'd
ever trash-talk a superior.

00:15:08.037 --> 00:15:09.212
Are you kidding me?

00:15:09.255 --> 00:15:10.735
Don't even get me started
on Stevens.

00:15:10.778 --> 00:15:12.911
Do you know he keeps a log
about his mustache?

00:15:15.696 --> 00:15:17.872
Gah, this isn't gonna hold
much longer!

00:15:17.916 --> 00:15:21.137
If I had thought for one second
before I hit that stupid vacuum,

00:15:21.180 --> 00:15:22.399
none of this
would have happened.

00:15:22.442 --> 00:15:24.357
No, it was my call
to go this way.

00:15:24.401 --> 00:15:26.011
I led us into this mess.

00:15:26.055 --> 00:15:29.058
Great. So, then, what, neither
of us should be in charge?

00:15:29.101 --> 00:15:31.190
-Oh.
-Ha!

00:15:31.234 --> 00:15:33.845
-Rutherford, Tendi.
-What do you two
think we should do?

00:15:33.888 --> 00:15:36.674
-We two?
-I-I don't know,
this isn't really my...

00:15:36.717 --> 00:15:40.069
Well, actually,
these are Excalbian bones.

00:15:40.112 --> 00:15:42.810
With enough friction, they
break down and become acidic.

00:15:42.854 --> 00:15:44.595
Which we could use
to cut through the wall paneling

00:15:44.638 --> 00:15:46.379
and access
the engineering sub-conduits.

00:15:46.423 --> 00:15:47.859
And those run
the length of the ship.

00:15:47.902 --> 00:15:49.600
Honestly, we could've bypassed

00:15:49.643 --> 00:15:51.254
all this scary stuff
by using them from the start.

00:15:51.297 --> 00:15:53.038
What?! Why didn't you
say something before?

00:15:53.082 --> 00:15:54.997
Because you guys were in charge.

00:15:55.040 --> 00:15:56.781
-Uh...
-Uh...

00:16:00.306 --> 00:16:02.700
There. This will buy us
some time, but not much.

00:16:02.743 --> 00:16:04.789
&lt;i&gt;Riker to away team.
-Go ahead.&lt;/i&gt;

00:16:04.832 --> 00:16:06.965
We've entered the system. What
the hell happened down there?

00:16:07.009 --> 00:16:09.663
Long story, sir.
Requesting emergency transport.

00:16:09.707 --> 00:16:11.317
-Get them out of there.
-I can't, sir.

00:16:11.361 --> 00:16:13.015
-Why the hell not?
-There's some sort

00:16:13.058 --> 00:16:14.581
&lt;i&gt;of distortion field.&lt;/i&gt;

00:16:14.625 --> 00:16:16.409
&lt;i&gt;It must be interfering
with the transporter.&lt;/i&gt;

00:16:16.453 --> 00:16:19.195
That Varuvian explosion
must have released an ion cloud.

00:16:19.238 --> 00:16:21.458
&lt;i&gt;Hang in down there.
We'll figure this out.&lt;/i&gt;

00:16:21.501 --> 00:16:23.677
Get the saw!

00:16:23.721 --> 00:16:26.376
We need to hit the door
with the saw!

00:16:29.857 --> 00:16:31.990
I can't say this is
how I pictured going out,

00:16:32.034 --> 00:16:33.426
but I'll tell you what,

00:16:33.470 --> 00:16:35.341
there's no other blokes
I'd rather be with.

00:16:35.385 --> 00:16:37.213
This is what
we signed up for,

00:16:37.256 --> 00:16:38.866
to boldly go.

00:16:39.867 --> 00:16:40.912
Boimler?

00:16:40.955 --> 00:16:42.000
Uh...

00:16:42.044 --> 00:16:43.393
I'm sorry, I gotta be honest.

00:16:43.436 --> 00:16:45.482
I didn't join Starfleet
to get in phaser fights.

00:16:45.525 --> 00:16:47.266
I signed up to explore,

00:16:47.310 --> 00:16:49.312
to be out in space
making new discoveries

00:16:49.355 --> 00:16:51.140
and peaceful
diplomatic solutions.

00:16:51.183 --> 00:16:52.880
&lt;i&gt;That's&lt;/i&gt; boldly going.

00:16:52.924 --> 00:16:54.143
And you know what?

00:16:54.186 --> 00:16:55.666
I'd love to be
in a string quartet.

00:16:55.709 --> 00:16:57.233
I love that when Riker was
on the &lt;i&gt;Enterprise,&lt;/i&gt;

00:16:57.276 --> 00:16:58.843
he was out there jammin'
on the trombone

00:16:58.886 --> 00:17:01.367
and catching love disease
and acting in plays

00:17:01.411 --> 00:17:03.630
and meeting his identical
transporter clone Thomas.

00:17:03.674 --> 00:17:06.155
That stuff may not seem as cool
as what you guys do,

00:17:06.198 --> 00:17:08.113
but it's Starfleet all the way.

00:17:09.636 --> 00:17:11.334
Ha-ha! Ho-ho-ho!

00:17:11.377 --> 00:17:13.684
I got into Starfleet
to study moss.

00:17:13.727 --> 00:17:16.382
I joined up
'cause I love beaming.

00:17:16.426 --> 00:17:18.384
Thanks, Boimler.
If we're going out,

00:17:18.428 --> 00:17:20.386
at least it's remembering
that Starfleet

00:17:20.430 --> 00:17:22.780
isn't just about kicking
enemy ass.

00:17:22.823 --> 00:17:25.870
Can't believe the captain has
a transporter clone.

00:17:25.913 --> 00:17:27.698
Yeah, Thomas Riker--
he was created

00:17:27.741 --> 00:17:29.917
from a distortion field
that was actually a lot like...

00:17:31.223 --> 00:17:32.137
What are you doing?

00:17:32.181 --> 00:17:33.660
We might not have to die!

00:17:37.360 --> 00:17:39.449
-Ah.

00:17:41.886 --> 00:17:43.888
Ha-ha! Yeah!

00:17:45.455 --> 00:17:47.892
Okay, the escape pods
should be down this way,

00:17:47.935 --> 00:17:49.154
if that's still the plan.

00:17:49.198 --> 00:17:50.895
It is if you say it is, buddy.

00:17:50.938 --> 00:17:53.202
Stay alert, stay alive.

00:17:53.245 --> 00:17:55.117
-Damn!
-Damn!

00:17:55.943 --> 00:17:58.511
&lt;i&gt;Captain, it's okay
if you want to check in&lt;/i&gt;

00:17:58.555 --> 00:18:00.383
-on Lieutenant Kayshon.
-No, no, no, no.

00:18:00.426 --> 00:18:02.733
I can be a hands-off captain.

00:18:02.776 --> 00:18:03.864
I don't mind.

00:18:03.908 --> 00:18:05.823
Captain,
two escape pods just launched

00:18:05.866 --> 00:18:08.739
-from the collector's ship.
-What?! On screen.

00:18:10.393 --> 00:18:11.742
What the hell is going on?

00:18:11.785 --> 00:18:14.092
&lt;i&gt;The ship tried to collect us,
Captain.&lt;/i&gt;

00:18:14.136 --> 00:18:15.311
Where's Kayshon?

00:18:15.354 --> 00:18:17.574
&lt;i&gt;Kayshon,
when he became a puppet.&lt;/i&gt;

00:18:17.617 --> 00:18:20.142
This is what being hands-off
gets me?

00:18:20.185 --> 00:18:22.927
Well, never again!

00:18:30.064 --> 00:18:31.588
Initiating drill.

00:18:31.631 --> 00:18:34.199
Reversing the polarity.

00:18:34.243 --> 00:18:35.679
I got signal lock.

00:18:35.722 --> 00:18:37.376
Get them out of there!

00:18:44.296 --> 00:18:46.124
Whoa, no. No, no, no, no.

00:18:52.391 --> 00:18:53.566
&lt;i&gt;-RIKER&lt;/i&gt;

00:18:53.610 --> 00:18:55.307
&lt;i&gt;-Boimler!
-Ah. Huh?&lt;/i&gt;

00:18:56.526 --> 00:18:57.483
Oh, God.

00:19:02.227 --> 00:19:03.881
The distortion field's
reengaging.

00:19:03.924 --> 00:19:05.665
-I'm losing him.
-That's not an option!

00:19:05.709 --> 00:19:06.884
Rerouting main power.

00:19:06.927 --> 00:19:08.755
Initiating second containment beam.

00:19:13.673 --> 00:19:15.588
Well done, Mr. Boimler.

00:19:15.632 --> 00:19:17.329
Thank you, Riker--
I mean, Mr. Captain.

00:19:17.373 --> 00:19:19.070
Get him to sickbay,
have the doc check him out.

00:19:19.113 --> 00:19:21.028
Riker to bridge.
Give me warp

00:19:21.072 --> 00:19:23.030
-in the factor
of five, six, seven...
Captain,

00:19:23.074 --> 00:19:25.511
shuttle craft incoming
from the planet, it's...

00:19:25.555 --> 00:19:27.383
-ours.
-What? That's not possible.

00:19:27.426 --> 00:19:28.949
We all beamed off.

00:19:28.993 --> 00:19:30.386
&lt;i&gt;Shuttle pilot's in distress.&lt;/i&gt;

00:19:30.429 --> 00:19:32.344
&lt;i&gt;-Requesting transport.
-Could be a Pakled trap.&lt;/i&gt;

00:19:32.388 --> 00:19:33.519
Energize.

00:19:35.782 --> 00:19:37.828
-Mr. Boimler?
-You guys made it!

00:19:37.871 --> 00:19:39.873
Oh! The Pakleds got stuck
in the door, so I...

00:19:39.917 --> 00:19:42.615
Aw, man. A copy of me
got transported out?

00:19:42.659 --> 00:19:43.877
Boo.

00:19:43.921 --> 00:19:45.749
&lt;i&gt;I'm&lt;/i&gt; the transporter clone? Boo.

00:19:45.792 --> 00:19:47.620
The distortion field must've...

00:19:47.664 --> 00:19:49.970
Oh. I've heard this tune before.

00:19:50.014 --> 00:19:51.407
Let's hear it for the Boimlers!

00:19:51.450 --> 00:19:52.451
-Yeah!

00:19:57.717 --> 00:19:59.893
Meeting your exact copy
is never easy.

00:19:59.937 --> 00:20:01.199
Believe me, I know.

00:20:01.243 --> 00:20:03.070
Mr. Boimlers,
you showed great bravery

00:20:03.114 --> 00:20:05.203
-and ingenuity down there.
Thank you, sir.

00:20:05.247 --> 00:20:07.292
I just wish
I could keep both of you.

00:20:07.336 --> 00:20:09.381
Starfleet Command feels
our missions are too complex

00:20:09.425 --> 00:20:12.471
to have the added complication
of two identical crew members.

00:20:12.515 --> 00:20:15.474
I'm afraid one of you will have
to return to the &lt;i&gt;Cerritos...&lt;/i&gt;

00:20:15.518 --> 00:20:17.041
as an ensign.

00:20:19.478 --> 00:20:21.088
I should be the one to go.

00:20:21.132 --> 00:20:23.047
-Huh?
-All right, works for me.

00:20:23.090 --> 00:20:24.701
Whoa, whoa, whoa, wait.
I thought we were both

00:20:24.744 --> 00:20:26.398
gonna step forward,
and then, like, you'd go,

00:20:26.442 --> 00:20:28.444
-"Oh, I should be
the one to go."
-Nah. I'm good to stay.

00:20:28.487 --> 00:20:30.750
-But what was that nod?
-I don't know, I just thought

00:20:30.794 --> 00:20:32.012
we were doing a copy thing.

00:20:32.056 --> 00:20:33.362
But thanks, man,
that's really big of you.

00:20:33.405 --> 00:20:35.625
Hey, I wish I could be on a ship
that's exploring

00:20:35.668 --> 00:20:38.715
and solving science mysteries
instead of nonstop fighting.

00:20:38.758 --> 00:20:40.586
-Like on the &lt;i&gt;D?
-Exactly.&lt;/i&gt;

00:20:40.630 --> 00:20:41.848
Damn, do I miss that ship.

00:20:41.892 --> 00:20:43.502
Enjoy it while you have it,
Bradward.

00:20:43.546 --> 00:20:44.982
I will, sir.

00:20:45.025 --> 00:20:46.853
Hey, Cap, the name Brad

00:20:46.897 --> 00:20:48.290
just feels kind of "meh"
to me now.

00:20:48.333 --> 00:20:50.857
What do you think
of "William" Boimler?

00:20:50.901 --> 00:20:53.120
I love it!
Hey, you like Romulan ale?

00:20:53.164 --> 00:20:54.426
Ah, I can learn.

00:20:54.470 --> 00:20:56.863
Computer, play "Nightbird."

00:21:00.911 --> 00:21:03.348
Hey, &lt;i&gt;Enterprise.&lt;/i&gt;

00:21:03.392 --> 00:21:06.395
-You did good.
-Go boldly out there, mate.

00:21:12.226 --> 00:21:14.272
You think
we'll ever see him again?

00:21:14.316 --> 00:21:15.795
I do.

00:21:15.839 --> 00:21:17.797
'Cause, like, his clone's here.
We'll see him every day.

00:21:17.841 --> 00:21:19.190
-Whoa!
-Oh, yeah.

00:21:22.802 --> 00:21:26.110
This isn't my first
"guy got turned into a doll."

00:21:26.153 --> 00:21:27.894
He'll be back to normal
in an hour.

00:21:27.938 --> 00:21:29.374
Aw. Look at this little guy.

00:21:29.418 --> 00:21:31.463
I could use him
as puppet therapy.

00:21:31.507 --> 00:21:32.595
-Hey! Migleemo!
-Yeah?

00:21:32.638 --> 00:21:34.597
Read the sign!

00:21:36.860 --> 00:21:39.819
Whoa! Did you get
double promoted? Congrats!

00:21:39.863 --> 00:21:41.168
Huh? What do you mean?

00:21:41.212 --> 00:21:42.518
You got a whole new pip
right there.

00:21:42.561 --> 00:21:44.346
Nah, just a piece of corn.

00:21:44.389 --> 00:21:45.390
That's always happening.

00:21:45.434 --> 00:21:47.044
Half the time
when you see someone

00:21:47.087 --> 00:21:48.915
with the wrong amount
of pips around here,

00:21:48.959 --> 00:21:51.091
it's usually
just delicious street corn.

00:21:51.135 --> 00:21:52.441
-Want some?
-Sure.

00:21:52.484 --> 00:21:54.312
I had you wrong, Jet.
I thought you were

00:21:54.356 --> 00:21:56.836
another one of those try-hards
who only wants to rank up.

00:21:56.880 --> 00:21:58.838
But you love the job,
and I respect that.

00:21:58.882 --> 00:22:02.189
Thanks, Mariner.
It's the best job in the galaxy.

00:22:02.233 --> 00:22:03.930
You're a true Lower Decker, man.

00:22:03.974 --> 00:22:06.019
And something tells me
we're gonna make a great team...

00:22:06.063 --> 00:22:07.891
Oh, my God, it's Boimler!
It's my friend!

00:22:07.934 --> 00:22:10.023
-What are you doing here!?
-You're supposed to be
on the &lt;i&gt;Titan!&lt;/i&gt;

00:22:10.067 --> 00:22:11.460
I got transporter cloned.

00:22:11.503 --> 00:22:13.200
-Ha-ha! Pay up.
-Damn it!

00:22:13.244 --> 00:22:15.115
How did you possibly guess that?

00:22:15.159 --> 00:22:17.379
Oh, I don't know, it just seemed
like a Boimler thing to happen.

00:22:17.422 --> 00:22:20.077
Clone me's staying on the &lt;i&gt;Titan,
so here I am.&lt;/i&gt;

00:22:20.120 --> 00:22:22.209
Wow. If you think
you can leave us

00:22:22.253 --> 00:22:24.734
for the big time
only to come crawling back,

00:22:24.777 --> 00:22:26.692
you would be right about that!

00:22:26.736 --> 00:22:28.390
Get over here, man. Sit down!

00:22:28.433 --> 00:22:31.567
Oh, there's no room
for me to, um...

00:22:31.610 --> 00:22:34.004
-Oh. I'll let you all catch up.
-Ha-ha-ha!

00:22:34.047 --> 00:22:37.094
-I know you got, like,
a shared history and stuff...
-Oh, man, so much to tell you.

00:22:37.137 --> 00:22:39.966
-We just did a mission
on a collector's ship.
-Ooh! And our away team leader

00:22:40.010 --> 00:22:42.708
got zapped by a ray
and it turned him into a puppet!

00:22:42.752 --> 00:22:44.754
-What?!
-So, was the &lt;i&gt;Titan&lt;/i&gt;

00:22:44.797 --> 00:22:46.146
as awesome
as everybody says?

00:22:46.190 --> 00:22:47.452
Eh, it was a bunch
of complex characters

00:22:47.496 --> 00:22:49.236
thrown into heavily
serialized battles

00:22:49.280 --> 00:22:51.021
which always ended
in mind-blowing twists

00:22:51.064 --> 00:22:52.849
and made me question
the basic tenets of my reality.

00:22:52.892 --> 00:22:54.111
But who cares about that?

00:22:54.154 --> 00:22:55.460
Tell me more
about this puppet ray.

00:22:55.504 --> 00:22:57.331
That's the kind of stuff
I live for.

00:22:57.375 --> 00:22:58.463
Time for shots!

00:22:58.507 --> 00:23:00.073
All right! Shots! Shots!

00:23:00.117 --> 00:23:01.858
-Whoa!
-Yeah, go get 'em.
You have a lot of work

00:23:01.901 --> 00:23:04.382
-to do for abandoning me.
-You're not
letting that go, huh?

00:23:04.426 --> 00:23:06.428
-Nope.
-Yeah, so hurry up, huh?

